report=dict(status='experimental x87 metadata and explicit comparison-policy contracts pass; P3 remains open',metadata=metadata,observations=observations,independent_compare_c1=independent,runs=runs,source_sha256={path:sha(root/path) for path in ['native/semantics/X87_STATE.cpp.inc','native/semantics/X87_RAW.cpp.inc','native/semantics/X87_LOAD.cpp.inc','native/semantics/x87_metadata_fixture.cpp','native/semantics/x87_compare_c1_probe.cpp','tools/x87_metadata_experiment.py','tools/x87_compare_c1_probe.py']},policy_bits={'0':'image save pointers only when ES is set','1':'legacy image segment selectors serialize as zero','2':'instruction FDP updates only for a newly unmasked exception','3':'instruction FOP updates only for a newly unmasked exception','4':'comparison preserves C1 except on stack underflow; clear bit selects unconditional C1 clear','5':'comparison preserves OF/SF/AF; clear bit selects zeroing these flags','32..63':'explicit MXCSR supported-bit mask for images'},retained_failures={'metadata-v1':'116320 cases exposed C1 disagreement between unconditional clearing and this Intel CPU. Exact pointer/opcode fields and service contracts agreed. Earlier stack/fault fixtures always initialized C1 to zero and did not expose the disagreement.','metadata-v2':'Fixture compilation rejected a duplicate comparison_profile local; no execution occurred. Fixed fixture declarations in v3, then tightened documented preserved C0/C2/C3 and FNINIT reset checks in v4.'},primary_sources=['https://www.intel.com/content/dam/www/public/us/en/documents/manuals/64-ia-32-architectures-software-developer-vol-2a-manual.pdf','https://docs.amd.com/api/khub/documents/sfvvekC9mDflu6vd3R0NXA/content'],limitations=['Authored AOT only. No game code was executed or newly accepted.','Both pointer/opcode policies cross all four comparison C1/auxiliary-flag combinations: eight explicit profiles. 6029312 cases pass their selected contracts, not universal hardware equivalence.','232640 selected C1 policy deviations and 517208 selected OF/SF/AF policy deviations from this Intel host remain recorded and explained; overlapping categories must not be summed as unique cases.','Intel instruction documentation says to clear comparison C1, but both independent authored probes observe preservation except stack underflow. The independent environment setup uses no AOT, Remill or SEH.','AMD application documentation lists only ZF/PF/CF modified by these comparisons. The preserve-OF/SF/AF policy follows that document and is not verified on AMD Jaguar hardware. Neither profile choice resolves the separate unmasked-invalid comparison flag behavior uncertainty.','The same metadata helper now covers constants, exchange, register pop, unordered integer-flag comparison, raw transfers/sign/conditional and narrow loads. Other numeric producers remain unconverted. FNINIT resets external selector metadata after clearing saved pointers/opcode.','Earlier payload/fault regressions retain their original scope; their added metadata stubs do not claim independent metadata coverage. The new fixture checks exact PC/FOP, selector resets, call counts, profiles and compound ordering.','Full logical native pointers remain checked; hardware pointer comparisons retain the separately documented low32 limit. Undefined condition bits for ordinary stack producers remain excluded; comparison preservation and FNINIT reset are checked.','1379648 matched pending hardware/native faults do not establish PS4 exception delivery or native Windows guest unwind.','Numeric stores/arithmetic/FSCALE, MMX coherence and native import/callback/exception/control closure remain open.'],experimental_semantics='v26-compare-policy',experimental_compiler='v6-x87-opcode',accepted_semantics='v9-sqrt',accepted_compiler='v5',compiled_entries=21168,remaining_compiler_rejections=2,remaining_quarantined_entries=8,native_game_boot=False,native_port_playable=False)
